version: 1.2
desc: Fenced In (Classic Master Limiter RE-01 port) by chmaha
author: chmaha
tags: limiter mastering brickwall look-ahead
changelog:
  Larger default window (1050x276), matching the other Classic ports.
about:
  Look-ahead brickwall mastering limiter with a vintage flavour: one Threshold knob from -20 to 0 dB drives the
  signal into a three-stage gain envelope (3 ms look-ahead, 0.5 ms attack, programme-dependent release), a cubic
  overshoot clipper and a fixed output ceiling of 0.977 (-0.2 dBFS), with left and right gain-reduction LEDs.
  Classic Master Limiter RE-01 is AnClark Liu's reverse-engineered recreation of a free mastering limiter from the
  early 2000s; this port matches it exactly. Latency: 580 samples at every sample rate up to 192 kHz, reported to
  the host for delay compensation.
  Ported from Classic Master Limiter RE-01 by AnClark Liu (GPL-3.0-or-later) https://github.com/AnClark/ClassicMasterLimiter-RE01
  Title lettering drawn from the outlines of Cormorant Garamond by the Cormorant Project Authors (SIL Open Font License 1.1).
  JSFX version released under GPL-3.0-or-later
  Claude generated some of this code
